# Athena's Intern — Avionics Induction Task

A real-time data processing and onboard monitoring system designed to simulate depth-sensing navigation and prevent a ship from running aground. 

## 🚀 Project Overview

The objective of this project is to process incoming time-series depth sensor data recorded at one-second intervals to monitor the sea floor. Because real-world telemetry is inherently erratic, the core challenge involved building a pipeline to clean corrupted data, reduce random signal noise, and visualize the results dynamically.

## 🛠️ Features & Implementation

* **Data Extraction:** Developed a Python backend to extract, parse, and structure time-series depth data from raw sensor logs.
* **Signal Processing (Noise Reduction):** Implemented data-cleaning techniques and filtering algorithms to eliminate corrupted anomalies and smooth out random sensor noise.
* **Live Animation:** Built a dynamic, real-time monitoring dashboard using Python visualization libraries that updates the depth-time graph point-by-point every second.
* **Clean UI/UX:** Styled the visualization with clear indicators, labels, and axes for immediate decision-making.

## 💻 Tech Stack

* **Language:** Python
* **Libraries:** Matplotlib (Animation & Plotting), NumPy / Pandas (Data Handling) *[Feel free to adjust these based on your actual imports]*
